GLFW
Version: 3.5.1
Source: https://github.com/glfw/glfw
Source tag: 3.5.1

Build type: Static

linux_amd64:
- Target: Linux x86_64
- Compiler: GCC
- Build type: Release
- Shared libraries: disabled
- X11 backend: enabled
- Wayland backend: enabled
- Examples: disabled
- Tests: disabled
- Documentation: disabled
- Install files: enabled

win64_mingw:
- Target: Windows x86_64
- Compiler: MinGW-w64 GCC
- Cross compiler prefix: x86_64-w64-mingw32-
- Build type: Release
- Shared libraries: disabled
- Examples: disabled
- Tests: disabled
- Documentation: disabled
- Install files: enabled

Included files:
- Public GLFW headers for each platform
- libglfw3.a

Notes:
- Headers are stored separately for each platform to preserve the exact installed output of each target build.
- Static libraries are platform- and toolchain-specific.
- The Linux build includes both X11 and Wayland support.
- The Linux static library still relies on the corresponding system windowing and graphics libraries at final link/runtime.
- The Windows build is intended for MinGW-w64 x86_64 targets.
- GLFW is used as the platform/window/input backend for RmlUi integration.
- The bundled static library is intended for WFZ components and related tooling.

